12. **C12 — Explicit destruction, resource cleanup, draining and secret wiping. KEEP.**  
    **Relevant decisions:** [OD28](docs/decisions.md#od28), [OD59](docs/decisions.md#od59), [OD60](docs/decisions.md#od60), [Core Q2](docs/decisions.md#decided-2026-11-05-core), [information-flow decision](docs/decisions.md#decided-project-infoflow-2026-11-06).  
    Moving a value out of a heap, destroying its contents and releasing an external resource have different observable consequences. `drain` accounts for elements whose cleanup cannot be supplied by `Destroy`. Secret aggregate destruction additionally has an observable wiping obligation; scalar Copy secrets deliberately make a different guarantee.  
    **Proposed simplification:** retain one consuming `Destroy` protocol and ordinary explicit cleanup calls. **Lost if unified:** failure handling, ownership conservation or honest wiping guarantees. Likewise, keep point-local `assert … by …` distinct from function-level `#[proof]`: their evidence scopes differ.

One review-sheet correction matters independently: its expected-type account of enum arguments conflicts with [OD129](docs/decisions.md#od129), which says argument-based inference, otherwise explicit. Correcting that account would not revise the language.

ANSWER: STRONG=C1,C2; ASK=C3,C4,C5,C6
